acturer, to a trading blacklist. Several global companies have since suspended business with the Chinese firm, raising fears that the ban will seriously undermine China’s burgeoning chip industry. Meanwhile official Chinese news agency Xinhua said there were some “delusional” American politicians who thought they could curb China’s rise through limiting technology cooperation with China. Explainer: Can the US take back some control of rare earths from China? Hawkish state-run tabloid the Global Times ran a separate article saying the comments by the NDRC on Tuesday were a “clear signal” that it was only a matter of time for Beijing to play the “rare earths card” in its feud with the US. “China understands clearly that the complex global supply chain comprises industries from every country in the world,” it said. “If China cuts off the exports of rare earths to the US … then China will also suffer but the impact felt by the US would be much more serious. “We believe if the US continues to pile pressure on us, it would be just a matter of time that we will weaponise our [rare earths exports].” China was accused of making a similar move in 2010 when tensions with Japan rose over a territorial dispute in the East China Sea. Observers say Beijing risks undermining its trading reputation and other trading partners might suffer if China restricts exports of the minerals.\",\"articleSection\":\"Diplomacy\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Laura Zhou\",\"sameAs\":\"https://www.scmp.com/author/laura-zhou\"},\"dateCreated\":\"2019-05-29T16:57:53+08:00\",\"dateModified\":\"2019-05-30T09:37:33+08:00\",\"datePublished\":\"2019-05-29T17:30:09+08:00\",\"genre\":\"News\",\"hasPart\":{\"isAccessibleForFree\":\"False\"},\"headline\":\"China issues veiled rare earths threats after US ups trade war ante with Huawei blacklist\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-GB\",\"isAccessibleForFree\":\"False\",\"locationCreated\":{\"name\":\"Hong Kong\"},\"publisher\":{\"name\":\"South China Morning Post\"}}"
